@startuml
' Figure - State Machine Diagram: evidence lifecycle
!include _header.txt

[*] --> Collected : register

Collected     --> Submitted      : submit [custody record exists]
Submitted     --> UnderAnalysis  : begin analysis [analyst or above]
UnderAnalysis --> Transferred    : hand over [recipient entitled]
Transferred   --> UnderAnalysis  : resume analysis
UnderAnalysis --> Archived       : archive [integrity verified Intact]\n[administrator]
Transferred   --> Archived       : archive [integrity verified Intact]\n[administrator]
Submitted     --> Archived       : archive [integrity verified Intact]\n[administrator]

Collected     --> Flagged : integrity failed
Submitted     --> Flagged : integrity failed
UnderAnalysis --> Flagged : integrity failed
Transferred   --> Flagged : integrity failed
Archived      --> Flagged : integrity failed

Flagged --> UnderAnalysis : clear [administrator]\n[re-verified Intact]

Archived --> [*] : retained indefinitely

note right of Flagged
  Flagged is reachable from EVERY state but
  escapable from ONE, by an administrator, and
  only after re-verification. An item whose
  integrity has failed cannot quietly resume
  normal handling (DR-06).
end note

note left of Collected
  Every transition carries a required function
  and a set of preconditions. 14 transitions
  over 6 states, declared as a table rather
  than as branching code.
end note
@enduml
